  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{0}^{6}(8{t}^{2}-3t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{8{t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{8(6)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3(6)^{2}}{2}]-[\\frac{8(0)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3(0)^{2}}{2}] \\\\  & =[576-54]-0 \\\\  & =522.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=0$ and $t=6$ is $522.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
